Database Definition:
"An organised collection of data.A method to manipulate and access the data"

Database vs dbms:
Let suppose,we have our app.We need a medium to collect data from app and store it in database.That medium is dbms.(It can be postgresql,mysql,oracle etc).The combination of medium(postgresql,oracle,mysql) with database is known as dbms

RDBMS:
A type of database system that stores data in structured tables (using rows and columns) and uses sql for managing and querying data

Imp:Generally use a semicolon (;) at the end of each SQL statement.
Imp: Postgresql is in sensitive,you can write query in upper or lower case both

